.\" Manpage for iso-remaster
.\" Contact adrian@example.com for bug reports
.TH ISO-REMASTER 1 "2025-01-09" "arch-remaster" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
iso-remaster \- Build an archiso-style ISO from an existing Arch root filesystem

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iso-remaster
.RI --out <file.iso>
.RB [--from\ <rootfs>]
.RB [options]

.SH DESCRIPTION
iso-remaster creates a bootable ISO image from an existing Arch Linux root filesystem directory. It packages the rootfs as a compressed squashfs filesystem and builds a complete ISO with GRUB boot support. This tool is designed for snapshot/remaster workflows on a host system.

.SH REQUIRED OPTIONS

.TP
.BR --out <file.iso>
Output ISO path

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR --from <dir>
Root filesystem directory to snapshot (default: /). Example: /mnt/rootfs
.TP
.BR --arch <arch>
Architecture for the ISO (default: x86_64)
.TP
.BR --label <volid>
Volume label for the ISO (default: Arch-Live)
.TP
.BR --work <dir>
Work directory for temporary files (default: mktemp creates a temp dir)
.TP
.BR --comp <algo>
Squashfs compression algorithm (default: zstd). Supported: gzip, lz4, lzo, xz, zstd
.TP
.BR --kernel <path>
Path to kernel image (default: <from>/boot/vmlinuz-linux)
.TP
.BR --initrd <path>
Path to initramfs image (default: <from>/boot/archiso.img)
.TP
.BR --no-copytoram
Do not include copytoram in GRUB kernel cmdline
.TP
.BR -m , --no-md5sum
Skip MD5 checksum calculation. Can be stacked with other short options
.TP
.BR --verbose
Enable verbose output for debugging

.SH EXAMPLES

Create an ISO from the host root filesystem:
.RS
.PP
.nf
sudo ./iso-remaster --out ./archlive.iso
.fi
.RE

Create an ISO from a mounted rootfs:
.RS
.PP
.nf
sudo ./iso-remaster --from /mnt/arch-root --out ./archlive.iso
.fi
.RE

Create with custom label and compression:
.RS
.PP
.nf
sudo ./iso-remaster --from /mnt/arch-root --out ./archlive.iso \\
    --label MYARCH --comp xz
.fi
.RE

Skip MD5 calculation:
.RS
.PP
.nf
sudo ./iso-remaster --from /mnt/arch-root --out ./archlive.iso -m
.fi
.RE

With verbose output:
.RS
.PP
.nf
sudo ./iso-remaster --from /mnt/arch-root --out ./archlive.iso --verbose
.fi
.RE

.SH EXCLUDED DIRECTORIES
The following directories are excluded from the squashfs:
.br
proc, sys, dev, run, tmp, mnt, media, var/tmp, var/cache/pacman/pkg, lost+found

.SH REQUIREMENTS
The following programs must be available:
.br
mksquashfs, grub-mkrescue, xorriso, md5sum

.SH NOTES
If --from is omitted, it defaults to / (the host root filesystem). The script runs with `set -euo pipefail` for safety and will clean up temporary files on exit.

.SH AUTHOR
Written for the arch-remaster project.

.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at the arch-remaster project repository.
